diff - what changed between two files

SYNOPSIS
    diff OLD NEW

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the lines that differ, in the usual < and > form.

    Which lines correspond is decided by the longest common subsequence -
    the most lines appearing in both files in the same order - so a line
    inserted near the top does not make everything after it look changed.

    The table is O(n*m), which is the textbook algorithm and the reason
    there is a line limit. Real diffs use Myers' algorithm, which finds
    the same answer in O((n+m)d) where d is the size of the difference:
    much better when the files are similar, which they usually are.

SEE ALSO
    grep, cat, sort
